# gitleaks false positives, allowlisted by fingerprint.
#
# The CBD thesaurus identifies taxonomy terms by GUID. gitleaks' `generic-api-key` rule scores a bare
# GUID as high-entropy and flags it as a credential. These are public term identifiers, not secrets:
# every GUID below is already a key in the tracked `i18n/locales/en.json`, and the same values are served
# publicly by https://api.cbd.int/api/v2013/thesaurus.
#
# Scoped by fingerprint (file + rule + line) rather than by path or rule, so the rest of these files —
# and the rest of the repo — stay fully scanned.
#
# Added by p03-01 (BL-994). `identifier-labels.json` is generated; if it is ever regenerated the line
# numbers shift, the hook will flag the new lines, and these fingerprints should be refreshed rather
# than broadened.

